WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.130
It is time for Drew's News.

2
00:00:02.130 --> 00:00:03.770
Your good news machete

3
00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:07.031
for cutting your way through the thick forest news.

4
00:00:07.031 --> 00:00:12.031
(audience laughs)
(Drew makes cutting sounds)

5
00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:13.800
And with me at the desk

6
00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:15.880
is my favorite co-pilot, Ross Matthews.

7
00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:17.676
Hi, everybody! Hi!
(audience applauds)

8
00:00:17.676 --> 00:00:18.509
Slasher.

9
00:00:19.624 --> 00:00:21.170
(Ross and Drew make cutting sounds)

10
00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:22.870
Well, it's Women's History Month,

11
00:00:22.870 --> 00:00:25.610
and we're starting with a phenomenal woman

12
00:00:25.610 --> 00:00:27.900
who is very near and dear to this show.

13
00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:29.010
Gayle King.

14
00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:30.900
PopSugar just published Gayle's thoughts

15
00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:33.530
on why it's not so bad

16
00:00:33.530 --> 00:00:35.650
to put yourself first.

17
00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:37.380 line:15%
She says that girls are raised

18
00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:39.850 line:15%
to take care of everyone else before themselves,

19
00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:41.530 line:15%
and it took her many years,

20
00:00:41.530 --> 00:00:42.765 line:15%
all the way up to her divorce,

21
00:00:42.765 --> 00:00:46.360 line:15%
to realize selfishness can be a positive,

22
00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:47.570 line:15%
not just a negative.

23
00:00:47.570 --> 00:00:50.070 line:15%
And it is vital to prioritize yourself.

24
00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:51.547 line:15%
And Gayle says, quote,

25
00:00:51.547 --> 00:00:53.497 line:15%
"When you're happy with yourself,

26
00:00:53.497 --> 00:00:55.897 line:15%
"when you're happy with the job you're doing,

27
00:00:55.897 --> 00:00:57.737 line:15%
"you're a better person, period.

28
00:00:57.737 --> 00:00:59.427 line:15%
"And this makes you a better employee,

29
00:00:59.427 --> 00:01:01.187 line:15%
"which means you're certainly a better mother,

30
00:01:01.187 --> 00:01:03.420 line:15%
"which means you're certainly a better friend."

31
00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:05.221 line:15%
The gospel, according to Gayle.

32
00:01:05.221 --> 00:01:06.370 line:15%
(audience applauds)
(Ross laughs)

33
00:01:06.370 --> 00:01:07.320 line:15%
Right?
I love it.

34
00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:09.867 line:15%
If Gayle King says it.

35
00:01:09.867 --> 00:01:10.700
She's the best.

36
00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:11.550
And to read the full essay,

37
00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:13.260
go on PopSugar now.

38
00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:14.093
I love this.

39
00:01:14.093 --> 00:01:15.260
I did too, you know, when you think about,

40
00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:17.150
whenever you talk to somebody,

41
00:01:17.150 --> 00:01:19.100
who's maybe later in their life,

42
00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:20.247
and you say, "What would you tell

43
00:01:20.247 --> 00:01:21.680
"a younger version of yourself?"

44
00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:23.780
It's always to take it easy on myself,

45
00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:26.670
to be kinder to myself, to love myself sooner.

46
00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:29.040
And I just, I can't agree with Gayle more.

47
00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:31.450
The sooner you can do a little self care,

48
00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:33.010
and just nurture yourself,

49
00:01:33.010 --> 00:01:34.270
the better person you'll be.

50
00:01:34.270 --> 00:01:35.110
Ugh, I just struggle
(audience applauds)

51
00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:37.300
with the oxygen mask.

52
00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:38.133
Oh, that analogy.

53
00:01:38.133 --> 00:01:40.640
That analogy never does it for me.

54
00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:42.010
I'm like, we're not always like,

55
00:01:42.010 --> 00:01:43.520
in a plain crash scenario.

56
00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:46.560
I need like, a daily metaphor.

57
00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:48.590
That isn't so severe and intense

58
00:01:48.590 --> 00:01:49.650
like the oxygen mask.

59
00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:52.160
And then self care is a term

60
00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:53.630
that just feels too passive.

61
00:01:53.630 --> 00:01:56.420
It doesn't have that fight in it.

62
00:01:56.420 --> 00:01:58.090
I'm terrible at those things.

63
00:01:58.090 --> 00:02:01.590
But I like how she's not talking about

64
00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:04.210
necessarily pampering yourself.

65
00:02:04.210 --> 00:02:06.590
It's just prioritizing yourself.

66
00:02:06.590 --> 00:02:07.423
Well yeah,
(audience applauds)

67
00:02:07.423 --> 00:02:08.770
and I think you have to love yourself,

68
00:02:08.770 --> 00:02:11.750
and that's how you prioritize yourself.

69
00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:14.230
Synonymous with self-care

70
00:02:14.230 --> 00:02:16.320
can also be self-awareness.

71
00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:17.600
And not the ego kind.

72
00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:20.350
But the knowing what you need

73
00:02:20.350 --> 00:02:21.320
to take care of others.

74
00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:22.670
'Cause I love taking care of others.

75
00:02:22.670 --> 00:02:23.780
I'm really good at it.
You are.

76
00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:25.910
Not as great prioritizing myself.

77
00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:28.280
So read the full article on PopSugar

78
00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:29.470
and see what Gayle has to say.

79
00:02:29.470 --> 00:02:30.303
And thanks, Gayle.
(audience applauds)

80
00:02:30.303 --> 00:02:31.850
Thank you, we love you.

81
00:02:31.850 --> 00:02:33.060
All right.

82
00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:36.420
We also love, it is Design Week around here!

83
00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:39.170
So let's talk about where pop culture,

84
00:02:39.170 --> 00:02:40.003
something we love.

85
00:02:40.003 --> 00:02:40.836
Oh, I love it.

86
00:02:40.836 --> 00:02:43.070
Meets home decor, something else we love.

87
00:02:43.070 --> 00:02:44.170
We've already talked on the show here

88
00:02:44.170 --> 00:02:47.520
about how "Bridgerton" is inspiring interior design.

89
00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:49.284
Oh, we love "Bridgerton!"

90
00:02:49.284 --> 00:02:51.950
Oh my God, season two is coming out soon!

91
00:02:51.950 --> 00:02:52.970
Like, any second.

92
00:02:52.970 --> 00:02:54.260
I know!
I can't wait!

93
00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:55.477
It's crowning!

94
00:02:55.477 --> 00:02:58.890
(audience and Ross laugh)

95
00:02:58.890 --> 00:03:00.660
Oh, I'm so proud of you!

96
00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:01.560
Is that a double pun?

97
00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:05.690
Yeah, that is a double pun! Wow, Drew!

98
00:03:05.690 --> 00:03:06.759
Well, okay.

99
00:03:06.759 --> 00:03:08.791
There are other shows that are inspiring

100
00:03:08.791 --> 00:03:10.206
design out there.

101
00:03:10.206 --> 00:03:12.220
Apartment Therapy reports,

102
00:03:12.220 --> 00:03:14.420
an analysis of search data from the last year

103
00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:16.519
found one big show people are inspired by

104
00:03:16.519 --> 00:03:18.590
is the show "Sherlock."

105
00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:20.670
People are loving that Victorian furnishing,

106
00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:22.780
that, they call it clutter core design,

107
00:03:22.780 --> 00:03:25.380 line:15%
which is more is more kind of approach.

108
00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:27.840 line:15%
Cramming your space with vintage accessories

109
00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:28.780 line:15%
and trinkets.

110
00:03:28.780 --> 00:03:30.170 line:15%
That causes anxiety for me.

111
00:03:30.170 --> 00:03:32.310 line:15%
Too much, too much, too much.
(audience laughs)

112
00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:33.960 line:15%
It's true, you love a white box, Rossy.

113
00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:37.140 line:15%
I do, I loved the interior design of "Mad Men."

114
00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:39.210 line:15%
They say that one was a big influence as well.

115
00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:40.730 line:15%
Oh, very mid-century.

116
00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:41.563 line:15%
Yeah.

117
00:03:41.563 --> 00:03:43.670 line:15%
And now people are turning to "Friends"

118
00:03:43.670 --> 00:03:47.220 line:15%
for that 90's design aesthetic.

119
00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:48.410 line:15%
And I started thinking like,

120
00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:49.340 line:15%
what am I into now?

121
00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:51.620 line:15%
What's inspiring my design that I'm watching?

122
00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:53.340
And I watch, just the worst.

123
00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:54.173
I'm, you know...

124
00:03:54.173 --> 00:03:55.417
You watch "90 Day Fiance."

125
00:03:55.417 --> 00:03:56.300
"90 Day Fiance."
(audience laughs)

126
00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:57.870
I was thinking of like,

127
00:03:57.870 --> 00:03:59.830
what is my designer sense inspired by?

128
00:03:59.830 --> 00:04:01.373
Those little pods in "Love is Blind."

129
00:04:01.373 --> 00:04:03.749
(audience laughs)

130
00:04:03.749 --> 00:04:05.983
I kind of want my own pod now.

131
00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:08.870
Fun fact.
What?

132
00:04:08.870 --> 00:04:11.880
The kitchen here, the way I designed it with Tom and Mel,

133
00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:14.100
our production designers,

134
00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:17.994
I was inspired by "The Handmaid's Tale" kitchen.

135
00:04:17.994 --> 00:04:18.827
Ooh.

136
00:04:18.827 --> 00:04:20.230
Oh my gosh!

137
00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:24.510
All the shaker style that that show had,

138
00:04:24.510 --> 00:04:26.890
if you think of "The Handmaid's Tale" kitchen,

139
00:04:26.890 --> 00:04:28.260
and you look at our kitchen,

140
00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:30.515
it might be like, "Oh, right."

141
00:04:30.515 --> 00:04:33.098 line:15%
(upbeat music)

